# One-A-Day — Project Rules

## Python

### Style

- Formatter: `ruff format` (line length 88)
- Linter: `ruff check` — rule sets: E, F, I, UP, B
- Type hints required on all function signatures
- Use `from __future__ import annotations` in all modules
- Import order: stdlib → third-party → local (blank line between)
- Use `pathlib.Path`, not `os.path`
- f-strings only
- No mutable default arguments
- Prefer `httpx` over `requests`; `requests` banned in scrapers

### Docstrings

- Required on public functions and classes
- Google style
- One-liner for simple functions; multi-line for complex logic
- Skip on private methods unless non-obvious

## TypeScript

### Style

- ESLint + Prettier (config in `eslint.config.js`, `.prettierrc`)
- Strict mode (`"strict": true`)
- No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow
- Named exports only (exception: page components for router)
- Props interfaces: `<Component>Props`, same file as component
- API response types in `src/types/index.ts`

### Hooks

- Naming: `use<Resource>` (e.g., `useLeads`, `useInterests`)
- Return typed objects (not tuples) when >2 values
- Use TanStack Query for server state — no `useEffect` + `useState` for fetching

## Testing

### Backend Structure
```
tests/
├── conftest.py                 # Shared fixtures
├── fixtures/
│   ├── sample_leads.json
│   ├── sample_interests.json
│   └── sample_html/
├── test_scrapers/              # One file per scraper
├── test_services/
└── test_routers/
```

### Backend Categories

| Category | Scope | Mocking | Coverage |
|----------|-------|---------|----------|
| Unit | Single function | All external | 80% (services, scrapers) |
| Integration | Service + DB | HTTP only | 80% (services, scrapers) |
| Router | Request/response cycle | HTTP + external | 70% |

### Backend Rules

| Rule | Rationale |
|------|-----------|
| Mock all HTTP in scraper tests | No real network calls in CI |
| Use `responses` or `pytest-httpx` | Consistent mocking |
| Test scoring with explicit numerics | Core business logic |
| Use `pytest-asyncio` with `async_mode = "auto"` | Async router tests |
| Use `httpx.AsyncClient` for router tests | Full request/response |
| Fixtures for sample data in `conftest.py` | DRY, consistent test data |
| HTML snapshots in `fixtures/sample_html/` | Reproducible scraper tests |

### Backend Required Test Cases

#### Scoring (`test_services/test_lead_service.py`)

| Case | Input | Expected |
|------|-------|----------|
| Exact match | keyword in raw_text | 100.0 × weight |
| Partial match | related term | 0 < score < 100 |
| No match | unrelated text | 0.0 |
| Multiple interests | several keywords | weighted sum |
| Inactive interest | `active=False` | ignored |

#### Scrapers (`test_scrapers/test_*.py`)

| Case | Setup | Assertion |
|------|-------|-----------|
| Success | Mock 200 + valid HTML | Returns `list[CandidateLead]` |
| HTTP error | Mock 500 | Returns `[]` |
| Parse failure | Mock 200 + malformed HTML | Returns `[]`, logs warning |
| Rate limiting | Two rapid calls | Second call delayed |

#### Routers (`test_routers/test_*.py`)

| Endpoint | Case | Status |
|----------|------|--------|
| `GET /leads/today` | Lead exists | 200 |
| `GET /leads/today` | No lead | 404 |
| `POST /leads/generate` | Success | 201 |
| `POST /leads/generate` | Already exists | 409 |
| `GET /leads` | With pagination | 200, correct `total` |

### Frontend Structure

Tests colocated with components:
```
src/components/
├── LeadCard.tsx
├── LeadCard.test.tsx
├── InterestEditor.tsx
└── InterestEditor.test.tsx
```

### Frontend Rules

| Rule | Rationale |
|------|-----------|
| Use `@testing-library/react` | Standard, no shallow rendering |
| Mock API modules | No real HTTP |
| Test all field states | Cover nullables like `contact_hint` |
| Skip page component tests | Test composed components instead |

### Frontend Required Test Cases

| Component | Cases |
|-----------|-------|
| `LeadCard` | All fields rendered; missing `contact_hint`; source badge |
| `InterestEditor` | Add interest; edit; delete with confirm; weight bounds |
| `SourceToggle` | Enable/disable; last run status display |
| `LeadHistory` | List renders; pagination; empty state |

### Coverage Thresholds

| Target | Minimum |
|--------|---------|
| `app/services/` | 80% |
| `app/scrapers/` | 80% |
| `app/routers/` | 70% |

## Scraper Conventions

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| One class per file | Extends `BaseScraper` |
| Implement `fetch_candidates(config) -> list[CandidateLead]` | Required method |
| HTTP via `self._get()` only | Never `requests`, `httpx`, `urllib` directly |
| Stateless | No DB, no file I/O, no side effects |
| Config from `ScraperSource.config` | No hardcoded URLs or selectors |
| Return `[]` on total failure | Don't raise; pipeline handles partial results |
| Validate config at start | Fail fast on missing keys |
| Respect robots.txt | `_get()` checks automatically |
| No Playwright/Selenium | Unless JS required; document in config |

### Logging in Scrapers

| Level | Event |
|-------|-------|
| INFO | Starting source, completed with count |
| DEBUG | Individual page fetch |
| WARNING | Parse failure, missing element |

## API Conventions

| Aspect | Rule |
|--------|------|
| Prefix | `/api/v1/` |
| List response | `{ "items": [...], "total": n }` |
| Single response | Flat object |
| Error response | `{ "detail": "message" }` |
| Pagination | `?skip=0&limit=20` |
| Status codes | 200, 201, 404, 409, 422 |

### Router Rules

- Routers validate input, call services, return schemas
- No ORM queries in routers
- No business logic in routers
- Catch domain exceptions, translate to `HTTPException`

## Error Handling

| Layer | Raises | Catches |
|-------|--------|---------|
| Scrapers | `ScraperError` | — |
| `scrape_service` | — | `ScraperError` → log, continue |
| `lead_service` | `LeadExistsError`, `SourceNotFoundError` | — |
| Routers | `HTTPException` | Domain exceptions |
| Frontend | — | TanStack Query handles via `error` |

## Logging

| Level | Use |
|-------|-----|
| DEBUG | Detailed flow, page fetches |
| INFO | Start/end events, selections |
| WARNING | Parse failures, retries |
| ERROR | Unrecoverable failures |

### Rules

- Use `structlog`
- Bind context: `logger.info("event", key=value)`
- Never log PII
- Scraper logs include `source_name`

## Git Conventions

| Aspect | Rule |
|--------|------|
| Branch naming | `feat/`, `fix/`, `chore/` + short description |
| Commit messages | Imperative, present tense, 50 char max |
| Direct commits to main | Forbidden |
| `.env` | Never committed |
| Dependencies | Commit lock files when changed |
| Scope | One logical change per commit |

### Pre-commit Hooks

Config in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`:

- `ruff check` + `ruff format`
- `detect-secrets`

Run after cloning:
```bash
pre-commit install
```

## CI Requirements

| Check | Command | Pass Criteria |
|-------|---------|---------------|
| Backend tests | `pytest` | All pass |
| Backend coverage | `pytest --cov --cov-fail-under=80` | ≥80% on services/scrapers |
| Backend lint | `ruff check .` | No errors |
| Backend format | `ruff format --check .` | No diff |
| Frontend tests | `npm run test` | All pass |
| Frontend lint | `npm run lint` | No errors |
| Secrets | `detect-secrets scan` | None found |
| Branch | — | Up-to-date with main |

## Prohibited Actions

| Category | Prohibition |
|----------|-------------|
| HTTP in scrapers | No `requests.get()`, `httpx.get()`, `urllib` — use `self._get()` |
| Logic in routers | No ORM queries, no business logic |
| DB in scrapers | Scrapers receive config, return dataclasses |
| Raw storage | No HTML, no full page text, no email lists |
| Excess PII | Name, title, affiliation, URL, contact hint only |
| Multiple leads/day | Unique constraint enforced |
| Rate limit bypass | Never disable, even in dev |
| PII logging | Never at any level |
| TypeScript `any` | Never |
| Inline `fetch()` | Use `src/api/` functions |
| `useEffect` + `useState` for data | Use TanStack Query |
| Hardcoded scraper config | Use `ScraperSource.config` |
| Undocumented deps | Update `pyproject.toml` / `package.json` |
| Push to main | Use branches |
| Naive datetimes | UTC only in database |